  {
   "id": "cheney",
   "title": "Cheney's copying collector",
   "prompt": "<p>With heaps as in the previous problem (a dict from addresses to lists of referenced addresses), write <code>copy_collect(heap, roots)</code>, a copying collector using Cheney's algorithm. It returns <code>(new_heap, new_roots, forwarding)</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Live objects get new addresses 0, 1, 2, … in the order Cheney's algorithm copies them: first the objects the roots refer to, in root order, then the objects found while scanning to-space from the start, each object's references in order. An object already copied is not copied again: the reference is redirected to its new address.</li>\n<li><code>new_heap</code> maps each new address to the list of <em>new</em> addresses its object refers to.</li>\n<li><code>new_roots</code> is the list of roots updated to new addresses.</li>\n<li><code>forwarding</code> maps each live object's old address to its new one (the forwarding addresses).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Don't change <code>heap</code>, and don't use recursion. Raise <code>ValueError</code> for a dangling reference. In Lesson 8's example, with root → A, A → B and C, B → A, and D unreachable, A gets 0, B 1 and C 2.</p>",
   "starter": "def copy_collect(heap, roots):\n    pass\n",
   "hint": "<p>Keep <code>forwarding</code> and a list <code>order</code> of old addresses in copy order; to-space is that list. A helper <code>copy(a)</code> gives <code>a</code> the next new address (<code>len(order)</code>) if it has none yet, and returns its new address. Copy the roots; then, with <code>scan</code> starting at 0, while <code>scan &lt; len(order)</code>, translate the references of <code>order[scan]</code> with <code>copy</code> (which may add to <code>order</code>) and advance.</p>",
   "solution": "def copy_collect(heap, roots):\n    forward = {}\n    order = []\n\n    def copy(a):\n        if a not in heap:\n            raise ValueError(f\"dangling reference to {a}\")\n        if a not in forward:\n            forward[a] = len(order)\n            order.append(a)\n        return forward[a]\n\n    new_roots = [copy(r) for r in roots]\n    new_heap = {}\n    scan = 0\n    while scan < len(order):\n        old = order[scan]\n        new_heap[scan] = [copy(x) for x in heap[old]]\n        scan += 1\n    return new_heap, new_roots, forward\n",
   "tests": [
    {
     "label": "The lesson's example",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "heap = {\"A\": [\"B\", \"C\"], \"B\": [\"A\"], \"C\": [], \"D\": [\"C\"]}\nnew_heap, new_roots, fwd = copy_collect(heap, [\"A\"])\nassert fwd == {\"A\": 0, \"B\": 1, \"C\": 2}, fwd\nassert new_heap == {0: [1, 2], 1: [0], 2: []}, new_heap\nassert new_roots == [0]\nassert heap == {\"A\": [\"B\", \"C\"], \"B\": [\"A\"], \"C\": [], \"D\": [\"C\"]}, \"don't change the old heap\"\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Breadth-first order from the roots",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "heap = {7: [3, 9], 3: [5], 9: [5, 1], 5: [], 1: [7], 8: [8]}\nnew_heap, new_roots, fwd = copy_collect(heap, [7])\nassert fwd == {7: 0, 3: 1, 9: 2, 5: 3, 1: 4}, fwd\nassert new_heap == {0: [1, 2], 1: [3], 2: [3, 4], 3: [], 4: [0]}, new_heap\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Several roots, repeated roots",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "heap = {\"p\": [\"q\"], \"q\": [], \"r\": [\"p\"], \"s\": []}\nnew_heap, new_roots, fwd = copy_collect(heap, [\"r\", \"q\", \"r\"])\nassert new_roots == [0, 1, 0], new_roots\nassert fwd == {\"r\": 0, \"q\": 1, \"p\": 2}, fwd\nassert new_heap == {0: [2], 1: [], 2: [1]}, new_heap\nassert copy_collect(heap, []) == ({}, [], {})\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Dangling references",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "try:\n    copy_collect({1: [2]}, [1])\nexcept ValueError:\n    pass\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError(\"expected ValueError from copy_collect({1: [2]}, [1])\")\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Agrees with marking, on a long chain",
     "type": "assert",
     "hidden": true,
     "code": "n = 50_000\nheap = {i: [i + 1, 0] for i in range(n - 1)}\nheap[n - 1] = []\nheap[-1] = [5]\nnew_heap, new_roots, fwd = copy_collect(heap, [0])\nassert len(new_heap) == n and -1 not in fwd\nassert all(fwd[i] == i for i in range(n))\nassert new_heap[3] == [4, 0]\n"
    }
   ]
  }
